make a tough decision.The Bayou Sampler included : Creole Jambalaya,Red Beans & Rice ,Crawfish Etoufee and Chicken & Sau..."},{"business_id":"BsgcLUWlc6RvvBRiAPWj5w","review_id":"A2skL2Pw6XAlESEpv6zSwQ","date":"2016-02-14T00:27:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9359777569770813,"text_excerpt":"Great place, great food. Went here on Lundi Gras and it was a bit busy but there was still seating available. I wasn't sure about getting creole food on Magagize Street, so I decided to check the place out. The menu has lots of authentic creole dishes available and has a full bar. After seated, we get a little brown paper bag with 4 cut pieces of French bread and butter. I got the bowl of crawfish étouffée and a friend got the red beans and rice. Both were excellent. The wait staff were polite and I think the owner or GM was even helping out with the daily tasks. Clean, friendly, quick place to eat. I'm ready to try some other dishes at this place."},{"business_id":"BsgcLUWlc6RvvBRiAPWj5w","review_id":"1GnYqR0SAZffHwZANVsxkA","date":"2016-02-20T04:26:59","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.930020809173584,"text_excerpt":"Really enjoyed the food here! Was my first time eating here. (I had the Crawfish Étouffée). It was the best I've had ever!! Also tried the stuffed bell pepper which was ok. Service was a little slow, but they were really busy on a weekend night. Definitely will visit this place again."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"BsgcLUWlc6RvvBRiAPWj5w","photo_id":"d0xGpWU_4Su3u1YEsSx_BA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/d0xGpWU_4Su3u1YEsSx_BA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9315437078475952},{"business_id":"BsgcLUWlc6RvvBRiAPWj5w","photo_id":"z2REOCcVB-2iwQNKbrpo1g","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/z2REOCcVB-2iwQNKbrpo1g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9162970781326294},{"business_id":"BsgcLUWlc6RvvBRiAPWj5w","photo_id":"c5CKscsKaxPPrWx3pL86Sg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/c5CKscsKaxPPrWx3pL86Sg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.903101801872253